From b2937e05eddf3670be733a4df832bf330f33555c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
Date: Wed, 18 Feb 2026 00:08:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fortran: Avoid UAF on missing END BLOCK cleanup [PR122491]

In gfc_match_end cleanup for COMP_BLOCK, the parser freed the current
namespace immediately after a malformed END statement. That namespace can
still be referenced by parser state and code nodes during error recovery,
triggering heap-use-after-free with sanitizer-instrumented compilers.

Keep the existing recovery flow (unlink + unwind to parent state), but
defer namespace lifetime to normal block unwinding/cleanup.

	PR fortran/122491

gcc/fortran/ChangeLog:

	* decl.cc (gfc_match_end): Do not free current BLOCK namespace
	during malformed END cleanup.

Reported-by: Filip Kastl <fkastl@suse.cz>
Suggested-by: Jakub Jelinek <jakub@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
---
 gcc/fortran/decl.cc | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gcc/fortran/decl.cc b/gcc/fortran/decl.cc
index cb6bd6f8cc0..b5128580548 100644
--- a/gcc/fortran/decl.cc
+++ b/gcc/fortran/decl.cc
@@ -9267,7 +9267,8 @@ cleanup:
 	  ns = ns->sibling;
 	}
 
-      gfc_free_namespace (gfc_current_ns);
+      /* The namespace can still be referenced by parser state and code nodes;
+	 let normal block unwinding/freeing own its lifetime.  */
       gfc_current_ns = parent_ns;
       gfc_state_stack = gfc_state_stack->previous;
       state = gfc_current_state ();
-- 
